<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.berwilson.cron-curator</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>curl -sS -m 540 -H "Authorization: Bearer $(grep '^CRON_SECRET=' __APP_DIR__/.env.local | cut -d= -f2-)" http://localhost:3000/api/cron/curator</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    Weekdays at 6:20am local — fold what the correspondence says onto the
    records, so the 06:50 note and 06:45 text report a CURRENT picture.

    ⚠ IT CAN SIT IN THE CROWDED HOUR BECAUSE IT MAKES NO MODEL CALL. Every
    other job in this window holds LM Studio for a minute or more and the
    model serves one request at a time (§12), which is why the slots are
    spaced. This one is a read over 26 records and their already-extracted
    evidence — measured at about three seconds for the whole portfolio — so
    it costs the brief nothing and must run BEFORE the two messages that
    report what it changed.

      06:20  THIS            (a read, ~3s, no model)
      06:30  weekly brief    (Mondays only, one ~90s call)
      06:45  Pepper's text   (two assemblies, no model)
      06:50  Pepper's note   (one call per person)
      07:00  daily digest    (one call)

    No `?housekeeping=1` here — the duplicate fold is model-heavy and runs on
    its own agent at 23:10. Mixing them would put a 45-minute budget in front
    of the brief.

    Weekdays only, matching the note: the curator's whole output is a line in
    a message nobody is sent on a Saturday, and a change reported to nobody
    is the one failure this design must not have.
  -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>2</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>3</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>4</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>5</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-curator.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-curator.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
